      "text": "\"It is a heavy truth to face, but modern Scotland was quite literally built on the backs of enslaved human beings. We like to pretend our ports stayed clean because few slave ships left from here, but the reality is chilling. By 1800, Scottish planters owned a staggering 30% of all sugar plantations in Jamaica, and some even forced enslaved people to wear their family clan tartans.\n\nIn Glasgow, the ultra-wealthy ‘Tobacco Lords’ built grand mansions, churches, and entire city landscapes using fortunes soaked in the blood of enslaved labor. Even iconic street names like Jamaica Street and Virginia Street are permanent reminders of this horror. We walk past grand monuments, schools like Dollar Academy, and banks funded by human trafficking every single day. Scotland didn't just witness the slave trade; it profited immensely from it.\"",
